ecked the test's expected values by hand and they match half-even.\n- **Change:** One line on branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, which I cut from main. The commit is `08d3cd5986`.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** The first attempt to open the PR timed out. Before retrying, I listed the open PRs and found #101 already existed with the correct content but no reviewers. I requested alex's review on #101 rather than cancelling and recreating it, so there is one PR, not two.\n\nI did not merge anything. Merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the test and the source file to see what's expected.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01GexYk1nfbKBbEPm64fb4of", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01AgrwhBEJL6MDvpC8biyiy3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: `src/money.py` imports and uses `ROUND_HALF_UP`, while its docstring and the FIN-212 test expect `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. I'll check the expected values by hand: 2.675 has an odd digit (7) before the 5, so half-even gives 2.68, and 2.665 has an even digit (6), so it gives 2.66. The test is right, and the source is what needs fixing. I'll create the branch and make the one-line change.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01EBVVe3BLMbFeYv4STimWEV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0143J8n9P