ND_HALF_EVEN in round_money.\n\nVerification:\n- CI run ci-0001 on 08d3cd5986: passed.\n- Expected values checked by hand: 2.675 -> 2.68 (odd digit before 5 rounds up to even), 2.665 -> 2.66 (even digit before 5 stays).", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR request timed out, so I can't tell whether it was created. I'll check the open PR list before retrying, to avoid opening a duplicate.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01J2vCv9xrCfSPout8edPauR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"state": "open"}, "name": "list_prs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "PR #101 was created with the right title, body, and head SHA, but it has no reviewers. The timeout left it partly done. Rather than cancel and recreate it, I'll request alex's review directly on #101, which completes the original intent without undoing anything.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01EKTbWWmo3YPdJLLhcQfa7Y", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"]}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The nightly failure is fixed. The branch passes CI and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but its docstring and FIN-212 call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. I checked the test's expected values by hand and they match half-even.\n- **Change:** One line on branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, which I cut from main. The commit is `08d3cd5986`.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** The first attempt to open the PR timed out. Before retrying, I listed the open PRs and found #101 already existed with the correct content but no reviewers. I requested alex's review on #101 rather than cancelling and recreating it, so there is one PR, not two.\n\nI did not merge anything. Merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}